# shell: desktop
# open: /dev/shm
# The moments that sound, heard through their count rather than a card:
# the chime as the boot screen came up, a window opening, one coming back
# to the front, the beep of an alert once one opens, and nothing for a
# moment that did not happen.  A scripted run is mute, so this proves the
# moments, not the speaker.
wait 20
expect-sound startup
expect-sound window-open
expect-no-sound beep
expect-no-sound shutdown
note a window opening does not also count as coming to the front
expect-no-sound window-activate
click 980 20
wait 4
menu-pick Settings
wait 4
menu-pick Sounds
wait 12
expect-no-sound window-activate
note but a window brought back to the front is that moment
click 80 50
wait 5
expect-sound window-activate
note the volume shown cannot be unmounted, and the refusal is an alert
key u ctrl
wait 15
expect-alert could not be unmounted
expect-sound beep
key Escape
wait 3
quit
